---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Recording Acoustic Instruments and Strings — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"Microphones, rooms and acoustic instruments — including the string parts most production writing skips."}
  canonicalPath={"/recording/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .hub-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .hub-head h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .hub-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 58ch; }

  /* ---- hub signature ----
     Each hub opens on a diagram of its own discipline, so the five main
     sections stop reading as one template with different words. Line work
     only, one ember mark per figure, and hidden below 820px where the head
     needs its full width for type. */
  .hub-head__inner { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .hub-head__inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.62fr); }
  }
  .sig { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .sig { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; justify-items: end; }
    .sig svg { inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 320px; height: auto; }
    .sig rect, .sig circle { fill: var(--line-strong); }
    .sig path, .sig line { stroke: var(--line-strong); stroke-width: 1.25; }
    .sig .sig-empty { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
    .sig .sig-solid { fill: var(--ink-soft); }
    .sig .sig-mark { fill: var(--ember-bright); }
    circle.sig-mark { fill: none; stroke: var(--ember-bright); stroke-width: 2; }
    .sig .sig-play { stroke: var(--ember-bright); stroke-width: 1.25; }
    .sig figcaption {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
      letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted);
    }
  }

  .topics { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .topics li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .topics a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.375rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.5rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .topics a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .topics h3 { font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.05rem + 0.75vw, 1.625rem); letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .topics p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .topics a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 14rem) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; }
  }

  .feature__inner { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 940px) { .feature__inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr); } }
  .feature h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.15rem + 2.1vw, 2.75rem); max-width: 20ch; margin-top: 0.875rem; }
  .feature p { color: var(--dark-muted); margin-top: 1.125rem; max-width: 46ch; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .feature .meta { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .feature .link { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .feature .ph { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }

  .tail { display: grid; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .tail { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4.5rem; } }
  .glossary > div { padding-block: 1.125rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary dt { font-weight: 550; font-size: 1.0625rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .glossary dd { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 0.25rem; max-width: 54ch; }
  .related li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .related li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .related a {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: 1.125rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 500;
  }
  .related a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .related svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; flex: none; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="hub-head" data-od-id="hub-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="hub-head__inner">
        <div>
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ol>
            <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
            <li>Recording</li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <h1>Recording acoustic instruments</h1>
        <p class="lede">What happens before anything reaches the DAW. Microphone choice and placement, what a domestic room will and will not give you, and the acoustic instruments — strings in particular — that most production writing leaves out entirely.</p>
      </div>
        <figure class="sig" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 110" fill="none" role="presentation"><path d="M 21 96 A 19 19 0 0 1 59 96" fill="none"/><path d="M 2 96 A 38 38 0 0 1 78 96" fill="none"/><path d="M -17 96 A 57 57 0 0 1 97 96" fill="none"/><path d="M -36 96 A 76 76 0 0 1 116 96" fill="none"/><path d="M -55 96 A 95 95 0 0 1 135 96" fill="none"/><circle cx="40" cy="96" r="4" class="sig-solid"/><line x1="150" y1="96" x2="150" y2="42"/><circle cx="150" cy="38" r="5" class="sig-mark"/><line x1="0" y1="96" x2="196" y2="96"/></svg>
          <figcaption>Radiation</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="hub-topics" aria-labelledby="topics-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2 id="topics-title" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip-path:inset(50%)">Topics in this hub</h2>
      <ul class="topics" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Home studio</h3>
          <p>Getting a usable recording out of a room that was designed to be lived in rather than recorded in.</p>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Acoustic instruments</h3>
          <p>Placement and gain staging for sources that move, breathe and change timbre with dynamics.</p>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Strings</h3>
          <p>Viola, violin and small ensembles — the repertoire this publication actually records.</p>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Live and sampled</h3>
          <p>Choosing between a player and a library, and how to make the two sit together when you use both.</p>
        </a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-dark feature" data-od-id="hub-feature" aria-labelledby="feature-title">
    <div class="shell feature__inner">
      <div class="ph" data-reveal>
        <span class="ph__label"><strong>Photograph</strong> — microphone position, three marked distances<br>to be captured at 2400 × 1600</span>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
        <p class="kicker">Start here</p>
        <h2 id="feature-title">How to Record Viola at Home</h2>
        <p>Placement, the room treatment you can genuinely do in a flat, and the three microphone positions worth trying before anything else. Written from the session that produced the samples used elsewhere on this site.</p>
        <p class="meta"><span>One condenser</span><span>48 kHz / 24-bit</span><span>16 min</span></p>
        <a class="link" href="/publishing-roadmap/">Read the guide
          <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" data-od-id="hub-latest" aria-labelledby="latest-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="latest-title">Latest in Recording</h2>
        <p>Newest first. Distances, angles and gain figures are stated, not implied.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="index" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-07-28">28 Jul 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Live Strings vs Sample Libraries: When Each Works</h3>
            <p>Four passages, played and programmed, with the audio to compare and the real cost of each route.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Comparison · 12 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/recording/acoustic-instruments/recording-viola-at-home/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-07-11">11 Jul 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>How to Record Viola at Home</h3>
            <p>Placement, room treatment you can actually do in a flat, and the three positions worth trying first.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Recording · 16 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-06-19">19 Jun 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Microphone Placement for Small String Ensembles</h3>
            <p>Two players, four players, one room — where the spot microphones stop helping.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Recording · 14 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-06-02">02 Jun 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Layering Live Strings With Virtual Instruments</h3>
            <p>Making a recorded part and a sampled section sound like one section rather than two.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Arrangement · 13 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-05-14">14 May 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Treating a Room You Are Not Allowed to Modify</h3>
            <p>What actually helps when nothing may be screwed into a wall, ranked by how much it helps.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Home studio · 11 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--tight band-surface" data-od-id="hub-tail">
    <div class="shell tail">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:var(--t-h3);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Terms used across this hub</h2>
        <dl class="glossary">
          <div>
            <dt>Proximity effect</dt>
            <dd>The bass lift that appears as a directional microphone moves closer to a source — a tone control, once you know it is there.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Spot microphone</dt>
            <dd>A close microphone on one instrument within a wider setup, mixed under the main pair for definition.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Room mode</dt>
            <dd>A standing wave at a frequency whose wavelength fits a dimension of the room, making some notes far louder in some positions.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Gain staging</dt>
            <dd>Setting level at every stage so nothing clips and nothing sits so low that noise becomes audible later.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:var(--t-h3);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Related</h2>
        <ul class="related">
          <li><a href="/sound-design/">Sound Design
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
          <li><a href="/music-for-media/">Music for Media
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
          <li><a href="/resources/tools/note-frequency/">Note & Frequency calculator
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
          <li><a href="/music-production/">Production
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="relaunch-notice">
    <div class="shell relaunch">
      <p>Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026. Historical
         references are preserved for context.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">Read the history and relaunch note
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>